ure  on the local level from law enforcement  and from the school from the school  board and the superintendent to have  someone who in fact has been arrested  for soliciting sex from a minor  on staff for 20 months  and then to be arrested again and then  more time pass before they are finally  terminated from their position is beyond  belief and in fact when you couple that  with the experiences in northern  virginia from last year when i was a  candidate where we saw in loudoun county  a woman assaulted when the school board  in fact moved moved a student from one  school to another who had already been  accused and convicted of an assault this  is why parents are losing faith in  public schools this is why  last year all across virginia all across  virginia you saw parents matter signs  we are empowering parents in virginia  today we pass legislation to give them  the ability to make decisions with  regards to their children wearing a mask  or not to actually have visibility in  the classroom on the materials that are  being used  to make sure they're appropriate and  consistent with their values not the  teachers values but their values this is  about recognizing who has the strongest  role in educating children and it is  parents and then teachers  you know we have these very important  midterms coming up in around 80 days  obviously every candidate is going to  talk about record high inflation record  high gas prices open borders but i would  argue that you also showed the  importance in your race of talking about  what is happening in the school system  in the towns and cities they live in and  also simple things like law and order  safety and security for every citizen  be it in a town or a city and these  ought to be bread and butter issues that  republicans own and and run on in this  uh pro in this upcoming election would  you agree  yeah without a doubt and of course what  we saw last year was these kitchen table  issues have conservative solutions that